{"tool": "finish", "summary": "API requests that insert, update or delete a row in `users` or `feeds` now append a row to a new `audit_log` table, in the same statement or transaction as the change. The build and existing unit and integration tests pass; nothing exercises the new audit rows yet, so that behaviour is untested here.\n\n**Not covered:** `PUT /v1/feeds/refresh` and `PUT /v1/categories/{id}/refresh` write no audit rows. They only queue jobs; the worker pool updates the feeds after the response has gone out, using its own unaudited store. Say if you want those logged too \u2014 it means carrying the audit context through the job queue.\n\n**Schema (my choice, the task didn't specify one):** `audit_log(id, created_at, actor_user_id, request, table_name, row_id, action)`, added as a new migration. `request` is the method and path (e.g. `PUT /v1/feeds/3`), `action` is `create`, `update` or `delete`, and there are no foreign keys so rows survive the users and feeds they refer to. If the acceptance tests expect different column names, this is the place to adjust.\n\n**What gets logged:**\n- **Users:** create, update and delete through `/v1/users`.\n- **Feeds:** create, update, delete, and the synchronous refresh `PUT /v1/feeds/{id}/refresh` (including when it only records a fetch error).\n- **OPML import:** one row per feed created.\n- **Cascades:** deleting a category logs each feed removed with it; deleting a user logs the user and each of their feeds.\n- **Google Reader API:** subscribe, unsubscribe, rename, move and disable-tag are logged as well. I treated it as an API; that is an addition beyond `/v1`.\n\nLast-login updates during authentication are not logged, as specified. The web UI, CLI and background scheduler are also not logged, since they are not API requests.\n\nThe mechanism is `Storage.WithAudit(actorUserID, request)` in `internal/storage/audit.go`. One side effect: `RemoveCategory` now always runs in a transaction, including for the web UI.", "t": 1794462373.225}
{"tool": "_result", "name": "finish", "chars": 55, "t": 1794462373.225}
